            <ArticleTitle>Antidepressant Use Among Persons Aged 12 and Over:United States,2011-2014.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Key findings Data from the National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey ● During 2011-2014, 12.7% of persons aged 12 and over, 8.6% of males, and 16.5% of females took antidepressant medication in the past month. ● For both males and females, non-Hispanic white persons were more likely to take antidepressant medication compared with those of other race and Hispanic-origin groups. ● One-fourth of persons who took antidepressant medication had done so for 10 years or more. ● Antidepressant use increased from 1999 to 2014.</AbstractText>
